course: dictionary
lesson: 3301
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and ether is one of them. The clues around the word tell you which meaning to use. «Until 1846, when ether was shown working in Boston, most surgery was done on patients who were awake.» Here ether is a medicine that puts people to sleep, so it is the liquid, not the sky.
explain: Ether is a noun, and it is uncountable, so you cannot say two ethers, just some ether. In old science books, ether was an invisible substance that people thought filled space. Scientists tested this idea, found it was not true, and dropped it.
explain: Ether can also mean the clear sky, as in poems. In everyday talk, «into the ether» means lost or disappeared, especially online or on the radio. When you meet ether, ask which meaning fits the sentence, then check by swapping your meaning in.
fact: Ether can mean a colourless liquid with a strong smell that evaporates easily.
fact: Long ago, «ether» was used to put patients to sleep for operations.
fact: Long ago, people thought an invisible substance called ether filled space; experiments showed it does not exist.
fact: «Into the ether» means lost or disappeared, especially online or on the radio.
fact: In poetry, ether can mean the clear sky or the upper air.
exercise: «Until 1846, when ether was shown working in Boston, most surgery was done on patients who were awake.» What was ether used for in this sentence? | *To put patients to sleep for operations | To carry light across empty space | To cool down hot rooms | To mend broken bones in the sky
exercise: A message «vanished into the ether» means what? | *It was lost or disappeared | It was written in gold ink | It was sent to the top of a castle | It was read aloud on the radio
exercise: In a poem, «the lark rose into the ether» means the lark flew up into what? | A dark cave | A deep river | *The clear sky | A field of wheat
test: Which sentence describes the old science idea of ether? | *An invisible substance that people thought filled space, which experiments showed does not exist | A sweet food that children ate at parties | A loud bell rung on the hill | A stone found only in caves
test: Which description fits ether as a liquid? | Green, thick and sweet | Bright red, heavy and sticky | *Colourless, with a strong smell, and it evaporates easily | Loud and cold, like a wave
exam: In a story, «the message went into the ether» tells you what? | *The message was found in the sky | The message was sent to a faraway country | The message was read in a poem | The message was lost or disappeared
